 {
  "id": "wa_chianti_spire_lichen_bouquet",
  "name": "Lichen Bouquet (East Face)",
  "discipline": "alpine",
  "grade": "5.9",
  "verdict": "SUMMIT_ONLY",
  "state": "wa",
  "peak": {
   "id": "wa_chianti_spire",
   "name": "Chianti Spire",
   "lat": 48.553355,
   "lng": -120.590487,
   "elevation_ft": 8400,
   "region": "Washington Pass",
   "path": "usa.washington.wa_northwest.wa_hwy20_ncnp.wa_north_cascades.wa_sub_wapass.wa_silver_star_and_wine_spires.wa_chianti_spire"
  },
  "text": {
   "approach": "Identical to Rebel Yell. Drive SR 20 to Washington Pass, then about 4 miles east to a wide pullout on the south side of the highway near milepost 166, at roughly 4,250 ft (about 0.7 mile past the Cutthroat Lake road, about 2 miles east of the hairpin turn). No Northwest Forest Pass is required on the highway shoulder. Descend a steep, faint scree path about 300 ft to Early Winters Creek, cross on logs, then follow the climbers' trail steeply uphill to a wooded bench at 6,400-6,600 ft - the standard low camp, with a year-round spring about 200 yards north of the trail and a seasonal spring in the sandy gully above. Above the bench the trail fades; follow cairns up loose gullies, trending right and up, into the main gully below Burgundy Col at 7,800-7,950 ft. The gully holds a roughly 40-degree snow finger into midsummer. Roughly 3.5 miles and about 3,700 ft of gain to the col in 3-4 hours. From the col, descend 200-300 ft on the south side and traverse right beneath Burgundy Spire's east face on year-round snow with seasonal rock bands until Chianti's east face is in view. Rebel Yell's dihedral is the obvious feature on the right side of the face; Lichen Bouquet's ramp starts directly below the summit and leans left. Under an hour from the col.",
   "approach_logistics": null,
   "road": "{\"name\":\"SR 20 (North Cascades Highway / Washington Pass)\",\"status\":\"Paved two-lane state highway suitable for any passenger car; parking on the highway shoulder at a wide pullout near milepost 166. No forest-road driving involved.\",\"driveNote\":\"From Washington Pass drive about 4 miles east to a broad pullout on the south (right) side of the highway near milepost 166, at roughly 4,250 ft, directly across the valley from Silver Star Mountain - about 0.7 mile past the Cutthroat Lake road and about 2 miles east of the hairpin turn. Several smaller pullouts come first. From the east, a short drive",
   "overview": "A 5.9 line on the same east face as Rebel Yell, following a long left-leaning ramp into a left-facing corner and an offwidth, then crossing Rebel Yell and continuing to the notch between Burgundy Spire and Chianti, where a short pitch on the normal route reaches the summit.",
   "description": null,
   "descent": "Most parties on the east face descend the way Rebel Yell parties do: from the summit pedestal, scramble to the two-bolt anchor at the southeast base of the summit block and make four double-rope rappels with two 60 m ropes back to the snow at the base of the face, trending generally to the rappeller's right and pulling the ropes carefully - the flake and offwidth features snag ropes readily. The a"
  },
